	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Wailing Caverns are a maze of caves beneath the heart of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}. Their mouth opens in a rocky hill beside the {link:lushwater-oasis}Lushwater Oasis{/link}, south of the {link:the-crossroads}Crossroads{/link}. Steam bursts from cracks in their stone with a long and mournful cry, and from that cry they take their name. Underground rivers run through them for miles, and from their hidden springs rise the waters of the new oases. Something has gone wrong in the deep. The beasts of the caverns have turned savage and strange, the water carries a taint that spreads across the plains, and the druids who came here to heal the land now serve the sickness.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records how old the caverns are. What is known is that the {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} druid {link:naralex}Naralex{/link} came to them with a company of disciples. He meant to enter the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link} and, through its power and the springs of the caverns, to grow the dry {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link} back into the forest it had once been. He lay down to dream. His focus faltered, and serpentine visions crept into his thoughts. His dream became a nightmare, and he could not wake. Through his sleeping mind, the nightmare began to seep into the waking world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:naralex}Naralex{/link} still sleeps in the depths of the caverns, tossing in troubled sleep. Most of his disciples have been twisted into the {link:druids-of-the-fang}Druids of the Fang{/link}, who wear the shapes of serpents and guard their master's slumber against all who would end it. Their four leaders, the Fanglords, each hold a gem of the dream. Deviate raptors, serpents and faerie dragons have risen from the nightmare to haunt the tunnels, and shapeless ectoplasms drift through the dark.

The world above has begun to notice. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} druid {link:tonga-runetotem}Tonga Runetotem{/link} traced the taint of the oases to the caverns, and {link:hamuul-runetotem}Hamuul Runetotem{/link} saw the Druids of the Fang in his own dreams. {link:nara-wildmane}Nara Wildmane{/link} learned their faces and wants their gems. The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} apothecary {link:apothecary-zamah}Apothecary Zamah{/link} seeks the serpentbloom that grows in the depths. The goblins of {link:ratchet}Ratchet{/link} want the essence of the ectoplasms for their drinks, and a thief called Mad Magglish has fled inside with a stolen bottle of old port. A few disciples of Naralex remain true. One waits within the caverns for anyone strong enough to help him wake his master.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Caverns",
			text = [=[• {b}The Mouth.{/b} Two faithful disciples, Nalpak and Ebru, keep watch on the hill above the entrance. The druid Falla Sagewind waits nearby.
• {b}The Caves of the Fang.{/b} In the upper caves, {link:lady-anacondra}Lady Anacondra{/link} and {link:lord-cobrahn}Lord Cobrahn{/link} command the druids and their serpents.
• {b}The River.{/b} An old turtle, {link:kresh}Kresh{/link}, wanders the underground river, untouched by the nightmare.
• {b}The Deep Pits.{/b} {link:lord-pythas}Lord Pythas{/link} and {link:lord-serpentis}Lord Serpentis{/link} hold the lower chambers. The thunder lizard {link:skum}Skum{/link} and the guardian {link:verdan-the-everliving}Verdan the Everliving{/link} lurk in the far caves.
• {b}The Dreamer's Chamber.{/b} At the heart of the caverns, {link:naralex}Naralex{/link} lies in his fitful sleep. Beneath the murky water near him, something waits.]=],
		},
	},
})

